   "date": "2020-06-05T16:43:49Z",
   "subject": "xlim_tree changing the order of panels in facet_plot",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"text-align:left\">Hi all,</div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">Since updating to R v4.0.0 (and ggtree v2.3.0) when using facet_plot if I use xlim_tree to set the limits for my tree panel (as instructed <a href=\"https://guangchuangyu.github.io/2016/10/xlim_tree-set-x-axis-limits-for-only-tree-panel/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://guangchuangyu.github.io/2016/10/xlim_tree-set-x-axis-limits-for-only-tree-panel/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482046245000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1NTliR95Xr-wvAfI4eY6nR\">here</a>) or adding a layer to a panel (as <a href=\"https://guangchuangyu.github.io/2016/12/add-layer-to-specific-panel-of-facet_plot-output/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://guangchuangyu.github.io/2016/12/add-layer-to-specific-panel-of-facet_plot-output/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482046245000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0h2ZiJqGnxJqg-ruT5AJM9\">here</a>) the order of my panels changes.</div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">Recreating the issue using the example <a href=\"https://guangchuangyu.github.io/2016/12/add-layer-to-specific-panel-of-facet_plot-output/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://guangchuangyu.github.io/2016/12/add-layer-to-specific-panel-of-facet_plot-output/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482046245000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0h2ZiJqGnxJqg-ruT5AJM9\">here</a>, at first everything is plotted as expected:</div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><p style=\"clear:both;text-align:left\"><img style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/bioc-ggtree/attach/2bc4a5bd12795/facet_bug.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"facet_bug.png\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\"></p><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">When I add xlim_tree the order is changed (and also doesn&#39;t seem to change the tree limits):</div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">facet_plot(p+xlim_tree(3), panel = &#39;Stacked Barplot&#39;, <br>           data = df, geom = geom_barh,<br>           mapping = aes(x = value, fill = category),<br>           stat=&#39;identity&#39; ) <br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><p style=\"clear:both;text-align:left\"><img style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/bioc-ggtree/attach/2bc4a5bd12795/facet_bug1.png?part=0.2&amp;view=1\" alt=\"facet_bug1.png\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\"></p><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">The same happens if I add a horizontal line to the bar panel:</div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">mean &lt;- data.frame(x=mean(df$value), .panel=&#39;Stacked Barplot&#39;)</div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">facet_plot(p, panel = &#39;Stacked Barplot&#39;, <br>           data = df, geom = geom_barh,<br>           mapping = aes(x = value, fill = category),<br>           stat=&#39;identity&#39; )  +<br>  geom_vline(data=mean,<br>             color=&quot;black&quot;,<br>             linetype=&quot;dashed&quot;,<br>             aes(xintercept=x))</div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><p style=\"clear:both;text-align:left\"><img style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/bioc-ggtree/attach/2bc4a5bd12795/facet_bug2.png?part=0.3&amp;view=1\" alt=\"facet_bug2.png\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\"></p><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">Is anybody else experiencing this problem or is something going on at my end?</div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">Thanks,</div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">Rowena<br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
