    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"text-align:left\">Hi all,</div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">Since updating to R v4.0.0 (and ggtree v2.3.0) when using facet_plot if I use xlim_tree to set the limits for my tree panel (as instructed <a href=\"https://guangchuangyu.github.io/2016/10/xlim_tree-set-x-axis-limits-for-only-tree-panel/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://guangchuangyu.github.io/2016/10/xlim_tree-set-x-axis-limits-for-only-tree-panel/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482046254000&amp;usg=AOvVaw17uxCjc2TSiMr8swdWqlMh\">here</a>) or adding a layer to a panel (as <a href=\"https://guangchuangyu.github.io/2016/12/add-layer-to-specific-panel-of-facet_plot-output/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://guangchuangyu.github.io/2016/12/add-layer-to-specific-panel-of-facet_plot-output/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482046254000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0o7ecxlQd0AZyhY2It7zCW\">here</a>) the order of my panels changes.</div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">Recreating the issue using the example <a href=\"https://guangchuangyu.github.io/2016/12/add-layer-to-specific-panel-of-facet_plot-output/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://guangchuangyu.github.io/2016/12/add-layer-to-specific-panel-of-facet_plot-output/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482046254000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0o7ecxlQd0AZyhY2It7zCW\">here</a>, at first everything is plotted as expected:</div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><p style=\"clear:both;text-align:left\"><img style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/bioc-ggtree/attach/4948adca353ba/facet_bug.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1&amp;authuser=0\" alt=\"facet_bug.png\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\"></p><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">When I add xlim_tree the order is changed (and also doesn&#39;t seem to change the tree limits):</div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">facet_plot(p+xlim_tree(3), panel = &#39;Stacked Barplot&#39;, <br>           data = df, geom = geom_barh,<br>           mapping = aes(x = value, fill = category),<br>           stat=&#39;identity&#39; ) <br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><p style=\"clear:both;text-align:left\"><img style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/bioc-ggtree/attach/4948adca353ba/facet_bug1.png?part=0.2&amp;view=1&amp;authuser=0\" alt=\"facet_bug1.png\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\"></p><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">The same happens if I add a horizontal line to the bar panel:</div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">mean &lt;- data.frame(x=mean(df$value), .panel=&#39;Stacked Barplot&#39;)</div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">facet_plot(p, panel = &#39;Stacked Barplot&#39;, <br>           data = df, geom = geom_barh,<br>           mapping = aes(x = value, fill = category),<br>           stat=&#39;identity&#39; )  +<br>  geom_vline(data=mean,<br>             color=&quot;black&quot;,<br>             linetype=&quot;dashed&quot;,<br>             aes(xintercept=x))</div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><p style=\"clear:both;text-align:left\"><img style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/bioc-ggtree/attach/4948adca353ba/facet_bug2.png?part=0.3&amp;view=1&amp;authuser=0\" alt=\"facet_bug2.png\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\"></p><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">Is anybody else experiencing this problem or is something going on at my end?</div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">Thanks,</div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\">Rowena<br></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\n1. G Yu*. Using ggtree to visualize data on tree-like structures. Current Protocols in Bioinformatics. 2020, 69:e96. <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1002/cpbi.96\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/10.1002/cpbi.96&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482046254000&amp;usg=AOvVaw26pJR9kiaDvcsPFUk-Hzxk\">https://doi.org/10.1002/cpbi.96</a><br>\r\n2. LG Wang, TTY Lam, S Xu, Z Dai, L Zhou, T Feng, P Guo, CW Dunn, BR Jones, T Bradley, H Zhu, Y Guan, Y Jiang, G Yu*. treeio: an R package for phylogenetic tree input and output with richly annotated and associated data. Molecular Biology and Evolution. 2020, 37(2):599-603. <a href=\"http://dx.doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msz240\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://dx.doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msz240&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482046254000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kjeEUr0lPEootaIlOKMP9\">http://dx.doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msz240</a><br>\r\n3. G Yu*, TTY Lam, H Zhu, Y Guan*. Two methods for mapping and visualizing associated data on phylogeny using ggtree. Molecular Biology and Evolution, 2018, 35(2):3041-3043. <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msy194\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msy194&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482046254000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2eX0xzh6EtefZqrUGnaoor\">https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msy194</a><br>\r\n4. G Yu, DK Smith, H Zhu, Y Guan, TTY Lam*. ggtree: an R package for visualization and annotation of phylogenetic trees with their covariates and other associated data, Methods in Ecology and Evolution, 2017, 8(1):28-36. <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210X.12628\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210X.12628&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482046254000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2nPTh3XQKHMbbMjj4mkP1f\">https://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210X.12628</a><br>\r\n5. Book: <a href=\"https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482046254000&amp;usg=AOvVaw22LOUF0v9MmhEwo5IwWWM3\">https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/</a><br>\r\n--- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;ggtree&quot; group.<br></blockquote></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
